Local-first block outliner: index, search and query a graph of Markdown files

Usage: notatnik <COMMAND>

Commands:
  new-graph  Create a new graph folder (pages/, journals/, .notatnik/config.toml)
  index      Bring the index up to date (or rebuild it from scratch)
  search     Full-text search (diacritic- and case-insensitive; `proj*` = prefix)
  query      Run a query (text, or @file to read it from a file)
  backlinks  List everything that links to a page
  page       Print a page's parsed block tree
  check      Health check: parse problems, conflict copies, dangling block refs, re-IDs (exit 2 if any problem)
  rename     Rename a page and rewrite every reference to it
  watch      Watch the graph folder and print an update for every external change
  decrypt    Decrypt an encrypted backup (`*.zip.enc`) without the app
  verify     Check the server copy of a synced graph against the local folder, decrypting what is stored encrypted
  help       Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help     Print help
  -V, --version  Print version
